  "description": "Minnie Kidd House houses a Glaucoma technician-led clinic for eyes (ophthalmology) which is run by Guy’s and St Thomas’ NHS Foundation trust. At the clinic they diagnose, manage and treat all kinds of glaucoma.\nThe clinic wants to develop the type of ophthalmology treatment offered by introducing an eye injection treatment to treat retinal conditions and prevent sight loss and improve poor eyesight in patients.\nThe project will see the replacement of an existing disused kitchen turned into three individual treatment rooms enabled by extending the existing internal footprint to match the current external footprint at ground floor level.\nThe proposed plan at ground floor will be extended by approximately 12m² to the east. The extension will be to the line of the east façade stair wall within the confines of the building envelope line to the east, and to the line of the north external wall, similar to the position of the gate and bin store wall. It will be a single storey extension of internal accommodation. The accommodation will consist of three new treatment rooms for the ophthalmology department, from which the eye injection treatment will take place. This is to allow the clinic to offer better facilities for patients that it currently does not offer on site. \nThe proposed first floor plan will consist of roof area that will house a required air handling unit to service the three new treatment rooms. The external plant will be shrouded by an acoustic screen 2.8m high above the new single storey roof height.",
